  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a string `s`, find the **first** non-repeating character in it and output its index. If it **does not** exist, output `-1`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"leetcode\"\n\n**Output:** 0\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe character `'l'` at index 0 is the first character that does not occur at any other index.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"loveleetcode\"\n\n**Output:** 2\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"aabb\"\n\n**Output:** -1\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 105`\n* `s` is composed of only lowercase English letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
